{"id":"step:2607.26154v1:001","chain_id":"chain:2607.26154v1:closed-form","inputs":["assumption:2607.26154v1:measurement-set-normalized"],"outputs":["statement:2607.26154v1:sign-set-collapse"],"operation":"definition_expansion","justification":{"description":"Rewrite admissible signs as an affine binary code. A parity check occurs in a commuting context exactly when an inclusion-minimal Pauli product relation is Pauli-active."},"active_assumptions":["assumption:2607.26154v1:measurement-set-normalized"],"source_anchors":["anchor:2607.26154v1:binary-sign-code","anchor:2607.26154v1:relaxation-proofs"],"verification_records":["verification:2607.26154v1:source-freeze","verification:2607.26154v1:source-derivation-review"],"status":"PARTIALLY_VERIFIED"}
{"id":"step:2607.26154v1:002","chain_id":"chain:2607.26154v1:closed-form","inputs":["statement:2602.18939v1:reduced-polytope-vrep-normalized","statement:2607.26154v1:sign-set-collapse","statement:2607.26154v1:sign-relaxed-polytope"],"outputs":["statement:2607.26154v1:relaxation-exactness"],"operation":"logical_inference","justification":{"description":"With no sign parity checks, exact and relaxed vertex lists coincide. Conversely, an excluded sign pattern is a relaxed vertex outside the exact polytope."},"active_assumptions":["assumption:2607.26154v1:no-pauli-active-dependencies"],"source_anchors":["anchor:2607.26154v1:relaxation-proofs"],"verification_records":["verification:prototype:active-dependency-negative-control","verification:2602.18939v1:vrep-proof-audit","verification:2602.18939v1:vrep-repair-review"],"status":"BLOCKED"}
{"id":"step:2607.26154v1:003","chain_id":"chain:2607.26154v1:closed-form","inputs":["statement:2607.26154v1:sign-relaxed-polytope"],"outputs":["statement:2607.26154v1:relaxed-affine-span"],"operation":"linear_algebra","justification":{"description":"Every Pauli node lies in a maximal commuting context. Flipping only its unrestricted relaxed sign gives two vertices whose difference is 2e_i, so the affine hull contains every coordinate direction. The affine sum constraint gives the l1 lower bound."},"active_assumptions":["assumption:2607.26154v1:measurement-set-normalized"],"source_anchors":["anchor:2607.26154v1:relaxation-proofs"],"verification_records":["verification:2607.26154v1:source-derivation-review"],"status":"PARTIALLY_VERIFIED"}
{"id":"step:2607.26154v1:004","chain_id":"chain:2607.26154v1:closed-form","inputs":["statement:2607.26154v1:relaxed-affine-span","statement:foundation:finite-lp-strong-duality"],"outputs":["statement:2607.26154v1:relaxed-dual-vertex-form"],"operation":"theorem_application","justification":{"description":"The concrete relaxed primal is feasible and bounded, so standard finite-dimensional linear-program strong duality applies."},"active_assumptions":[],"source_anchors":["anchor:2607.26154v1:relaxation-proofs"],"verification_records":["verification:2607.26154v1:source-derivation-review"],"status":"PARTIALLY_VERIFIED"}
{"id":"step:2607.26154v1:005","chain_id":"chain:2607.26154v1:closed-form","inputs":["statement:2607.26154v1:relaxed-dual-vertex-form"],"outputs":["statement:2607.26154v1:dual-mwis"],"operation":"optimization","justification":{"description":"For fixed S, freely choose each relaxed sign to align with y and the global sign of mu, giving sum_(i in S)|y_i|+|mu|. Nonnegative weights make maximizing over maximal independent sets equivalent to maximizing over all independent sets."},"active_assumptions":[],"source_anchors":["anchor:2607.26154v1:dual-mwis","anchor:2607.26154v1:relaxation-proofs"],"verification_records":["verification:2607.26154v1:source-derivation-review"],"status":"PARTIALLY_VERIFIED"}
{"id":"step:2607.26154v1:006","chain_id":"chain:2607.26154v1:closed-form","inputs":["statement:2607.26154v1:relaxation-exactness","statement:2607.26154v1:dual-mwis"],"outputs":["statement:2607.26154v1:exact-graph-dual"],"operation":"substitution","justification":{"description":"The no-Pauli-active-dependency gate transfers the relaxed graph-only dual to the exact reduced robustness."},"active_assumptions":["assumption:2607.26154v1:no-pauli-active-dependencies"],"source_anchors":["anchor:2607.26154v1:relaxation-proofs"],"verification_records":["verification:2607.26154v1:source-derivation-review"],"status":"BLOCKED"}
{"id":"step:2607.26154v1:007","chain_id":"chain:2607.26154v1:closed-form","inputs":["statement:foundation:perfect-graph-weighted-duality"],"outputs":["statement:2607.26154v1:perfect-antiblocker-local"],"operation":"logical_inference","justification":{"description":"Weighted stable-set/fractional-clique-cover equality plus downward closure gives the target paper's clean antiblocker identity. This is target-local synthesis, not a verbatim imported theorem."},"active_assumptions":["assumption:2607.26154v1:perfect-frustration-graph"],"source_anchors":["anchor:2607.26154v1:perfect-antiblocker-report"],"verification_records":["verification:2607.26154v1:source-derivation-review"],"status":"BLOCKED"}
{"id":"step:2607.26154v1:008","chain_id":"chain:2607.26154v1:closed-form","inputs":["statement:2607.26154v1:exact-graph-dual","statement:2607.26154v1:perfect-antiblocker-local"],"outputs":["statement:2607.26154v1:closed-form-equality"],"operation":"optimization","justification":{"description":"The antiblocker representation bounds each feasible dual objective by a convex combination of 1 and clique sums. The feasible witnesses (y,mu)=(0,1) and clique-aligned (y_Q,0) attain the two branches."},"active_assumptions":["assumption:2607.26154v1:no-pauli-active-dependencies","assumption:2607.26154v1:perfect-frustration-graph"],"source_anchors":["anchor:2607.26154v1:closed-form-proof"],"verification_records":["verification:2607.26154v1:source-derivation-review","verification:prototype:finite-instances"],"status":"BLOCKED"}
{"id":"step:2607.26154v1:009","chain_id":"chain:2607.26154v1:capacity","inputs":["statement:2607.26154v1:closed-form-equality"],"outputs":["statement:2607.26154v1:clique-upper-bound"],"operation":"symmetry_or_conservation","justification":{"description":"For pairwise anticommuting P in Q, A=sum a_P P with unit Euclidean coefficients obeys A^2=I. Nonnegative variance gives the l2 bound on clique expectations, and Cauchy-Schwarz converts it to the l1 bound sqrt(|Q|)."},"active_assumptions":["assumption:2607.26154v1:rho-density"],"source_anchors":["anchor:2607.26154v1:closed-form-proof"],"verification_records":["verification:2607.26154v1:source-derivation-review","verification:prototype:finite-instances"],"status":"PARTIALLY_VERIFIED"}
{"id":"step:2607.26154v1:010","chain_id":"chain:2607.26154v1:capacity","inputs":["statement:2607.26154v1:clique-upper-bound"],"outputs":["statement:2607.26154v1:capacity-attained"],"operation":"constructive_witness","justification":{"description":"For a maximum clique Q, the equal-weight anticommuting sum is a traceless involution. A normalized state on its +1 eigenspace has every clique expectation 1/sqrt(|Q|), saturating the l1 bound."},"active_assumptions":["assumption:2607.26154v1:measurement-set-normalized","assumption:2607.26154v1:rho-density"],"source_anchors":["anchor:2607.26154v1:closed-form-proof"],"verification_records":["verification:prototype:finite-instances"],"status":"PARTIALLY_VERIFIED"}
